 ## Overview
-Orthographic projection is a size-preserving mapping that flattens a 3D scene onto a 2D plane such that objects in the foreground occupy the same screen space as identical objects in the background, and parallel lines in 3D remain parallel in the projection [S1, unofficial]. It differs from perspective projection, which creates depth by scaling objects smaller with distance [S2]. It is a sibling to [Viewing Plane Ray Generation](2424-viewing-plane-ray-generation.md) and builds on [Orthographic (Parallel) Camera Ray Generation](1319-orthographic-parallel-camera-ray-generation.md).
